.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-CA 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-ca
.Nd the machine's own certificate authority: one root, and the certificates it signs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Op Fl -force
.Nm
.Cm issue
.Ar name
.Op Fl -dns Ar host ...
.Op Fl -ip Ar address ...
.Op Fl -days Ar n
.Op Fl -eku Ar usages
.Nm
.Cm renew
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm info | dump-root | dump-der
.Nm
.Cm trust-install | enroll-mok
.Nm
.Cm sign-module
.Ar kernel-version
.Ar module
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Every kldload install makes its own certificate authority, once, while it
is installed: a root key and a ten-year root certificate under
.Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root .
It signs the web console's certificate, through
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8 ,
and a certificate for each virtual machine that vmxplore enrols.
Trusting the one root \(em in the system, in a browser, on another
machine \(em trusts all of them.
The root certificate is served at
.Lk https://host:8443/kldload-ca.crt
for that.
.Pp
The root's key is also the Secure Boot machine owner key:
.Xr kldload-secure-boot 8
enrols it and signs kernel modules with it.
.Pp
A new install makes a new root; a machine that is wiped and reinstalled
does not share a trust root with what it replaced.
Every command but
.Cm info ,
.Cm dump-root
and
.Cm dump-der
needs root.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init Op Fl -force
Make the root, if there is none; otherwise show it, as
.Cm info
does.
With
.Fl -force ,
move the existing root aside to
.Pa root.archived\&. Ns Ar YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS
and make a new one.
Certificates already issued stay signed by the old root;
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8
re-issues the console's on its next run.
.It Cm issue Ar name Oo Fl -dns Ar host Oc ... Oo Fl -ip Ar address Oc ... Op Fl -days Ar n Op Fl -eku Ar usages
Make a key and a certificate for
.Ar name ,
signed by the root and valid for each
.Ar host
and
.Ar address ,
for
.Ar n
days (default 90), for the extended key usages given (default
.Ql serverAuth,clientAuth ) .
They are written to
.Pa leaves/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .key
and
.Pa .crt ,
replacing any from before.
.Ar name
is letters, digits, dots, dashes and underscores, starting with a letter
or digit.
The arguments are saved for
.Cm renew .
.It Cm renew Ar name
Issue
.Ar name
again with the arguments it was last issued with.
.It Cm info
The root's fingerprint, subject and validity, and every certificate
issued with its expiry.
.It Cm dump-root , Cm dump-der
Print the root certificate, as PEM or as DER.
.It Cm trust-install
Add the root to the system trust store, with the tool this distribution
has
.Po
.Xr update-ca-trust 8 ,
.Xr update-ca-certificates 8
or
.Xr trust 1
.Pc ,
and, where
.Xr certutil 1
is installed, to the browser store of every ordinary user
(uid 1000 and up) whose home exists.
It fails if no system store could be updated.
First boot runs it.
.It Cm enroll-mok
Queue the root for Secure Boot enrolment with
.Xr mokutil 1 ,
unless it is enrolled or queued already; the next boot stops in
MokManager to confirm it.
The password is
.Ev KLDLOAD_MOK_PASSWORD ,
or
.Ql kldload .
Nothing in kldload calls this;
.Xr kldload-secure-boot 8
does the enrolment itself.
.It Cm sign-module Ar kernel-version Ar module
Sign a kernel module with the root key, using that kernel's
.Pa sign-file ,
for use as DKMS's signing helper.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help , Cm help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_CA_DIR
Where the authority lives, instead of
.Pa /etc/kldload/ca .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_MOK_PASSWORD
The one-time password MokManager asks for.
A password set here is not written to the log; the default is.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root/ca.key
The root key, mode 0600.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root/ca.crt , Pa ca.der
The root certificate, readable by anyone.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root/fingerprint , Pa serial , Pa ca.conf , Pa openssl.log
Its SHA-256 fingerprint, the serial counter, the request
.Cm init
made, and
.Xr openssl 1 Ns 's
messages.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/leaves/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .key , Pa .crt
An issued key, mode 0640, group root, and its certificate.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/leaves/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .sans , Pa .cnf
The arguments
.Cm renew
replays, and the request.
.El
.Pp
The directories are
.Pa /etc
and not
.Pa /var/lib
because
.Pa /var/lib/kldload
is a dataset of its own, mounted at first boot over whatever the
installer wrote there.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Done, or nothing to do.
.It 1
An error, named on standard error.
.It 2
No command, or an unknown one.
.El
